WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 8.12 · Marketing & Communications
Reputation, crisis communication and social media policy

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
Prepare roles and words before a crisis; in one, put people’s safety first.

3
00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:15.600
1. List likely scenarios and who leads each one.

4
00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:18.200
2. Draft holding statements and who must be told.

5
00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:22.200
3. Agree social media rules for staff and volunteers.

6
00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:23.800
An example: Riverside Repair Hub (Hybrid · charity with a trading company, United Kingdom)

7
00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:31.000
“Unsafe item sold: Tom leads with Helen; similar items withdrawn; trustees, company board and insurer told within 24 hours.”

8
00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:33.400
You write crisis scenarios and social media rules.

9
00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:37.400
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

10
00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:42.000
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
